      "writtenOn": "2023-12-21T22:48:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Pretty sure this is a no-op in this position and can be removed; `inline` (confusingly) is now about linkage, not the inliner. If you think this isn\u0027t being inlined but ought to be, we could copy this macro from Chrome: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/base/+/master/compiler_specific.h#63\n\nWe have very similar needs in Raster Pipeline and elsewhere so maybe it\u0027s time for a shared `SK_ALWAYS_INLINE`. (We have `SI` in SkRasterPipeline_opts.h)\n\nOr, we could just use `[[clang::always_inline]]` here since we don\u0027t really care much about winning benchmarks in GCC anyway.",
